# Data Leak Analysis & Least Privilege Controls (NIST SP 800-53 AC-6)

## Overview
An incident response analysis of an internal data leak caused by unrevoked folder access and accidental public sharing. The activity focuses on applying the Principle of Least Privilege and implementing NIST SP 800-53 (AC-6) access control enhancements to mitigate unauthorized exposure of sensitive assets.

## Incident Summary
* **Cause:** Unrevoked internal folder permissions coupled with human error led to an internal product folder link being shared externally and posted publicly on social media.
* **Core Issue:** Excessive access privileges and reliance on manual warnings rather than technical access boundaries.

## Controls & Recommendations (NIST SP 800-53 AC-6)
* **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):** Restrict access to sensitive internal assets strictly to authorized roles (e.g., managers and designated product leads).
* **Automated Expiration:** Implement automated access revocation mechanisms for shared resources after specified timeframes or meetings.
* **Privilege Auditing & Logging:** Maintain activity logs of provisioned accounts and perform regular audits of user access levels.

## Concepts & Skills Demonstrated
* Data Leak Prevention (DLP)
* Principle of Least Privilege (NIST SP 800-53: AC-6)
* Access Control & Authorization Policies (RBAC)
* Risk Mitigation & Security Awareness
